<h2>Évaluation de l'accessibilité</h2>

<p>Instruction</p>
<ol>
	<li>Définir la porté de l'évaluation</li>
	<li>Choisir un ensemble de règle pour la conformité à l'accessibilité tel que disponible dans le <a href="https://github.com/wet-boew/act-rules/">dépôt des règles ACT de WET-BOEW</a></li>
	<li>Compléter les informations suivante dans le gabarit d'évaluationt utilisé:
		<ul>
			<li>Sujet <code>earl:subject</code></li>
			<li>Votre nom et votre organisation <code>earl:assertedBy</code></li>
			<li>Date <code>dct:date</code></li>
		</ul>
	</li>
	<li>Ajouter l'ensemble du gabarit JSON des règles dans la propriété <code>earl:result</code></li>
	<li>Pour chaque <code>earl:result</code>, mettez à l'essai, évalué et noté le résultat obtenu par rapport au test associé à la règle d'essaie de conformité à l'accessibilité <code>earl:test</code></li>
	<li>Finaliser l'évaluation en y ajoutant une note sommaire <code>dct:description</code></li>
</ol>

<h2>Production du rapport de conformance à l'accessibilité</h2>

<p>Cette section et ses sous-sections nécessitent une traduction.</p>
<div lang="en">
	<ul>
		<li><a href="#acr-init">Report initialization</a></li>
		<li><a href="#acr-audit">Auditing and referencing an assessment</a></li>
		<li><a href="#acr-issuing">Issuing and formalizing the ACR report</a></li>
		<li><a href="#acr-archiving">Archiving</a></li>
	</ul>

	<h3 id="acr-init">Report initialization</h3>
	<ol>
		<li>Define the evaluation scope</li>
		<li>Choose a conformance criteria ruleset published in the <a href="https://github.com/wet-boew/act-rules/">WET-BOEW ACT rules repository</a></li>
		<li>Complete following information in the assessment report template:
			<ul>
				<li>Subject <code>earl:subject</code></li>
				<li>Your name and your organization <code>earl:assertedBy</code></li>
				<li>Date created <code>dct:created</code></li>
				<li>Conformance to standard <code>acr:standard</code></li>
				<li>Conformance option <code>acr:conformanceOption</code></li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Set the selected ruleset JSON template as baseline in <code>acr:conformityCriteria</code></li>
	</ol>

	<h3 id="acr-audit">Auditing and referencing an assessment</h3>
	<ol>
		<li>Edit the living ACR where the new assessment are in-scope of the tested subject</li>
		<li>Add the referenced assesment in <code>acr:assessment</code>
			<ul>
				<li>The key is the URL where the assessment in JSON could be retreived</li>
				<li>Add the assessment title <code>dct:title</code></li>
				<li>Add a link to the HTML equivalent report <code>dct:references</code></li>
				<li>Define the main language used for that assessment (2 letter code) <code>dct:language</code></li>
				<li>Set the date of when assessment was added into this ACR <code>dct:date</code></li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Make the assessment audit <code>acr:audits</code>
			<ul>
				<li>Your name <code>earl:assertedBy</code></li>
				<li>Define the testing mode <code>earl:mode</code></li>
				<li>Add a reference to the assessment <code>acr:assessment</code></li>
				<li>Audit each evaluated test case and record your finding if applicable in <code>acr:auditNotes</code>
					<ul>
						<li>Define the accuracy (False negative, False positive, Accurate) in <code>acr:accuracy</code></li>
						<li>Set the date of this note <code>dct:date</code></li>
						<li>Set the title of this note <code>dct:title</code></li>
						<li>Associate the applicable test case <code>earl:test</code></li>
						<li>Describe the concern expressed by this note <code>dct:description</code></li>
						<li>Describe the error message if applicable <code>earl:info</code></li>
						<li>Optional, define a severity level <code>acr:severity</code></li>
						<li>Optional, define a relevancy subject <code>acr:relevancy</code></li>
						<li>Optional, include an attachment encoded in data URL <code>acr:asset</code></li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>If applicable, create work item <code>acr:workItem</code> and for each work item:
					<ul>
						<li>Set the title <code>dct:title</code></li>
						<li>Describe the work objective and concern to provide enough context. <code>dct:description</code></li>
						<li>Add a reference to the discussion page <code>dct:references</code></li>
						<li>Set the work item creation date <code>dct:created</code></li>
						<li>Define the test requirement this work item is about <code>dct:created</code></li>
						<li>Define the test case this work item is about <code>acr:requirement</code></li>
						<li>Define the specific test case this work item is about <code>earl:test</code></li>
						<li>Optional, define a severity level <code>acr:severity</code></li>
						<li>Optional, define a relevancy subject <code>acr:relevancy</code></li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>Update the conformity of the criteria affected by the assessment and for each updated conformance requirement:
					<ul>
						<li>Update the conformance state (Satisfied, Not satisfied, Further test needed) <code>acr:conformance</code></li>
						<li>Add a reference to the applicable assessment <code>acr:assessment</code></li>
						<li>Add a description about its latest conformance state, if applicable <code>dct:description</code></li>
						<li>Update the modified date <code>dct:modified</code></li>
						<li>Define the cumulative testing mode for this conformance requirement conformity <code>earl:mode</code></li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li>If possible, add your verifiable credential</li>
	</ol>

	<h3 id="acr-issuing">Issuing and formalizing the ACR report</h3>
	<ol>
		<li>Edit the living ACR for which we want to set the conformance status for the tested subject</li>
		<li>Validate the integrity of the test subject for all related assessment and audits. If this is not satisfied, the ACR must be archived.</li>
		<li>Revise audits, work items and all conformance requirement to ensure they are accurate.</li>
		<li>Validate each conformance requirement, none of them should be marked as "Further test needed"</li>
		<li>Set your name and your organization name as the main assertor name for the conformance report <code>earl:assertedBy</code></li>
		<li>Define the conformance report conformance where it is "satisfied" only and only if all the conformance requirement are also "satisfied". Otherwise it is "not satisfied".</li>
		<li>Set the current date as the issue date <code>dct:issued</code></li>
		<li>If possible, add your verifiable credential</li>
	</ol>

	<h3 id="acr-archiving">Archiving</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>For each <code>earl:result</code>, assess, test and notes the result according to the associated accessibility conformance testing rule <code>earl:test</code></li>
		<li>Finalize the assessment by adding an assessment summary in <code>dct:description</code></li>


		<li>When we don't know it's replacement
			<ol>
				<li>Edit the ACR report to archive</li>
				<li>Set the expiry date of when the ACR was officially acknowledged to be outdated <code>schema:expires</code></li>
				<li>If possible, add your verifiable credential</li>
			</ol>
		</li>
		<li>It's being replaced by a new report
			<ol>
				<li>Edit the ACR report to archive</li>
				<li>If not defined, set the expiry date of when the ACR was superseded <code>schema:expires</code></li>
				<li>Set the URL of the replacement ACR report <code>dct:isReplacedBy</code></li>
				<li>If possible, add your verifiable credential</li>
			</ol>
		</li>
		<li>
			<p>When the ACR report are reissued.</p>
			<p>Note: Reissued accessibility conformance report must have its own identities which must be different of the issued accessibility conformance report. Which means in practice the creation of a new JSON file for the reissued ACR report.</p>
			<ol>
				<li>Issue the reissued ACR as an independent report by including a reference to its previous version <code>dct:isVersionOf</code></li>
				<li>Edit the ACR report to archive</li>
				<li>If not defined, set the expiry date of when the ACR was reissued <code>schema:expires</code></li>
				<li>Set the URL of the reissued ACR report <code>dct:hasVersion</code></li>
				<li>If possible, add your verifiable credential</li>
			</ol>
		</li>
	</ul>
</div>

